{
  "about": "The input-form descriptors the two Pipelex SDKs must both refuse: what each makes of a pipe I/O answer (POST /v1/pipe-io) whose input_form entry for the selected pipe is malformed where preparation reads it. 'answer' is a well-formed valid answer selecting 'pipe_ref', whose entry declares a document, a prose, an object nesting an image, and a list of documents; both SDKs prepare against it. Each case replaces answer.input_form[pipe_ref] with 'entry', the base entry with one thing wrong, and 'path' is where in the entry the refusal points, the empty string for the entry itself. A malformation is the route breaking its contract, so both SDKs refuse every case with a runtime verdict that is not retryable, before anything is uploaded: @pipelex/sdk's prepareInputs throws an InputPreparationError naming the pipe_ref and the path, and pipelex-sdk's client raises an ApiResponseError when it parses the answer, before prepare_inputs walks anything. A shape only one SDK refuses, such as a member the standard does not define, stays out of this file. This file exists twice: js/tests/fixtures/malformed-input-forms.json is the source, and python/tests/fixtures/malformed-input-forms.json its copy, which must stay byte for byte identical. Change the source, then run make shared-files at the repository's root to write the copy; make check-shared-files fails on a stale one.",
